<%
  content_for :page_title, "Privacy Policy | #{domain_name}"
  content_for :meta_description, "How The Greatest LLC collects, uses and safeguards your information across its sites."
%>

<%# One policy for all three sites -- The Greatest LLC operates them together
    and handles data the same way on each, so a per-site copy would be three
    documents to keep true instead of one. Only the site name changes, and it
    comes from domain_name so this reads correctly on whichever host serves it. %>
<article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
  <div class="prose max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p class="lead">Last updated: <%= PagesController::LAST_UPDATED.to_fs(:long) %></p>

    <p>
      Welcome to <%= domain_name %> ("we", "us", "our"). Your privacy is important to us, and we are
      committed to safeguarding your personal information. This Privacy Policy ("Policy") describes how
      we collect, use, disclose and safeguard your information when you visit our sites.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Greatest LLC operates thegreatestbooks.org, thegreatestmusic.org and thegreatest.games
      (each a "Site", together the "Sites"), including any related media form, media channel, mobile
      website or mobile application. This Policy applies to all of them. One account works across
      every Site, so information you give us on one Site may be visible to you on the others.
    </p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

    <h3>Personal Information</h3>
    <p>
      When you register for an account you may be asked to provide your name, email address and other
      identifiable information. You are also able to build a profile, which may include additional
      personal information such as the titles you have rated, reviewed, or added to your lists.
    </p>

    <h3>Non-Personal Information</h3>
    <p>
      Like most websites, we also collect non-personal information through cookies, log files and
      third-party analytics tools. This information may include your IP address, browser type,
      operating system and browsing history on the Sites.
    </p>

    <h3>Information from Third Parties</h3>
    <p>
      We may also receive information from third-party partners, such as advertisers, and from the
      sign-in provider you choose when you create an account.
    </p>

    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To personalize your experience</li>
      <li>To improve our Sites</li>
      <li>To send periodic emails</li>
      <li>To serve targeted advertisements</li>
      <li>To process membership payments and donations</li>
      <li>To fulfill other purposes for which you provided the information</li>
      <li>For analytics and research</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Disclosure of Information</h2>
    <p>We may disclose information:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>To third-party service providers</li>
      <li>To comply with legal requirements</li>
      <li>In case of a business transfer such as a merger or acquisition</li>
      <li>To enforce our Sites' policies</li>
      <li>To protect our or others' rights and safety</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>
      Membership payments and donations are processed by Stripe. We do not receive or store your card
      number. Stripe's handling of that information is governed by its own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We use cookies to compile aggregate data about site traffic and site interactions in order to
      offer better site experiences and tools in the future. You can choose to have your computer warn
      you each time a cookie is being sent, or you can turn off all cookies through your browser
      settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      We may use third-party advertising companies to serve ads when you visit our Sites. These
      companies may use information about your visits to these and other websites to provide relevant
      advertisements about goods and services that may interest you.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      We implement a variety of security measures to maintain the safety of your personal information.
      However, no electronic storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute data security.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting Your Account</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us to delete your account and the personal information associated with it at any
      time. See our <%= link_to "Deletion Policy", deletion_policy_path %> for how to make that request.
    </p>

    <h2>Updates to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Policy from time to time. Any updates will be effective upon posting the
      updated Policy on this page, and we will update the "Last updated" date above.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>For any questions regarding this Policy, you may contact us at <%= mail_to SiteContact::ADDRESS %>.</p>
  </div>
</article>
